WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah. Yeah, I got multiple
notifications on LinkedIn

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people working in the
prime minister's office

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.710
were looking at my profile.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.313
More than once I got
these notifications.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.515
And the first time I was like,
"Okay, what does that mean?"

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.384
Then the second time
and the third time.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it was clear to me
that I had said some things

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:97% position:3%
that were not so good for
their public relations team.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.597
(suspenseful music)

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.502 line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin,

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.804 line:0%
and joining me today is
the Substack essayist

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:41.374 line:0%
for "Noble Truths with
Rav Arora" and journalist

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.710 align:start size:84% position:16%
who I don't have to
put air quotes around.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.978
It's quite lovely.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.547
Rav Arora, welcome back
to "The Rubin Report."

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.782
- Hey, Dave.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.749
It's good to be on,

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.084
and it's good to get that formal

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.386
"Noble Truths with Rav
Arora" introduction.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.088
I'm still working
on that branding,

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.825
but I like the way you said
it, for sure. Appreciate it.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.895
- "Noble Truths with Rav
Arora," it sounds pleasant

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.831
and lofty and really
the highest compliment

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.399 align:start size:81% position:19%
that I can give
someone these days

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.134
the fact that I can
call you a journalist

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.602
and I didn't have
to do air quotes.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.138
I mean, does it get
any better than that?

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.373
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.208 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I don't have any
formal education.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:18.478
So, for some people that
evokes a lot of skepticism

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:22.449 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
about who this weirdo writing
in his mom's basement is,

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:25.819 line:0%
but I think for a lot of people,

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.354
I just kind of just
say what I wanna say.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I'm just straight
with the facts

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.092
and I don't try to spin it

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.828
according to any kind of
precondition narrative.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.296
I'm not working for anybody.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:39.632 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm just writing about issues
that are important to me.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.035
And I don't really identify
as liberal or conservative,

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.003
just kind of trying to
make sense of the world,

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.505
whatever comes my way.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if that means I'm
gonna sound a little left

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.442
on something or a little
right, I just go for it.

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.879
- Well, Rav, I would
rather have a weirdo

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
in his mom's
basement than someone

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.050
that went to Columbia
Journalism School,

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.785
so you are good to go.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:88% position:13%
Most of my audience
probably recognizes you.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.921
You've been on the show

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:05.325
for multiple Friday
panel extravaganzas,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.993 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you do find work
as a journalist.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.661
You are up in Canada.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.863
And the reason I wanted to do

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:12.332 align:start size:88% position:13%
this condensed interview
with you today,

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.567
and we're just sort of
shooting this on the fly

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.137 align:start size:88% position:13%
is because you've gotten
into some hot water

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:21.541 align:start position:0%
with your prime minister up
there in Canada, Justin Trudeau.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:88% position:13%
In my estimation is
the most authoritarian,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:29.249
I would say world leader
from a Western nation.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.451 align:start size:88% position:13%
And you've been
writing a bit about him

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:32.719
and what's going on in Canada.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:35.588
And now the government
is looking into you.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.957
You scary person in
your mom's basement.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.192
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.693
I don't know why
I'm so threatening.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.763 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I don't know, my mom
has been funny about this

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I can talk about
that in a second.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:49.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
But yeah, I wrote an op-ed
in the "New York Post"

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:53.606
calling Trudeau basically a
horrible authoritarian leader

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's violated basic human
rights, civil liberties

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.612
and constitutional rights,

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.415
specifically with respect
to the vaccine mandates.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.617
And I just talked about how

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.686 align:start size:84% position:16%
my family were
immigrants from India

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:10.557
and we came to Canada in
search for more freedom.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:14.961 align:start size:97% position:3%
Whether that's financial,
social, political, vocational.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.462 align:start size:84% position:16%
We just wanted
more opportunities.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.232
And that was kind of the idea
that my mom and my dad had,

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.868
is to give us more
freedoms, right?

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.036
Give their kids more freedom,

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.405 align:start size:88% position:13%
so they can pursue
what they wanna pursue.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:84% position:16%
And here we are during
the COVID pandemic.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.344
And, yes, there are many issues

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.646
surrounding keeping people safe,

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.715
keeping vulnerable people safe.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:39.085 align:start size:84% position:16%
And there are various
restrictions that
perhaps make sense.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.788
But when it came
to just my freedom,

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.723
it was completely restricted.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.825 align:start size:88% position:13%
I couldn't go to the gym
for the longest time,

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.060
for several months.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.529
Couldn't go out to a
restaurant and dine in,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I couldn't
even travel by air.

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:54.067
I couldn't even fly
or go on a train

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.903
anywhere in the country,
let alone leave the country

00:03:56.903 --> 00:04:01.774
for several months due to
the travel vaccine mandates

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:05.545 align:start size:97% position:3%
that outright discriminated,
outright banned

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:08.147
the unvaccinated from
traveling anywhere,

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.749 align:start size:84% position:16%
other than if you
wanna go in your car.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:13.152
But even that you couldn't
cross the US-Canada border.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:16.189
And I missed out on a
lot of opportunities.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.124
Like in December, for example

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:21.094
I was talking to
Ben Shapiro's team.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.629 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've been on a
show a couple times

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.330
and we were thinking about
doing something in Florida

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.099 line:0%
actually at the time in person.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.534 line:0%
And I just couldn't go
because I was banned.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:32.538 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I was deemed as a
second-class citizen

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.374
who was not able to travel.

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.842 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so, in this
article that I wrote,

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:39.479 align:start size:84% position:16%
I just made that
point of in many ways

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:43.549
my freedoms would've been
more secured in India,

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.418
the country that I
came from than here.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.654 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even though we came
here for more freedoms.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:52.325 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that to me is
just a total travesty

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.327
and really makes us reevaluate

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:58.398 align:start size:84% position:16%
what this supposedly
free liberal democracy
here in Canada,

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:01.434
where our freedoms are
completely restricted.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.736
- So, you write the piece
in the "New York Post."

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.271 align:start size:84% position:16%
And of course,
nothing you're saying

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.973 align:start size:88% position:13%
is coming as a
surprise to my audience

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.541
because obviously
we've covered a lot

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.310 align:start size:88% position:13%
of what's going on with
Trudeau and Canada,

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
the trucker convoy and
freezing of bank accounts,

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.480
and all of that stuff.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I think everyone
watching this is on board.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.484
They hear what you're saying.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:21.020 align:start size:84% position:16%
But then how did
this thing level up?

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.723 align:start size:84% position:16%
You suddenly found
some government people

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.491 align:start size:84% position:16%
were doing a little
digging on you.

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.860
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got multiple
notifications on LinkedIn

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people working in the
prime minister's office

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.502
were looking at my profile.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.005
More than once I got
these notifications.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.074
And the first time I was like,
"Okay, what does that mean?"

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:43.142
And the second time
and the third time.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:48.147 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it was clear to me
that I had said some things

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:52.719 align:start size:97% position:3%
that were not so good for
their public relations team.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:55.121
And I don't know who it
was that looked at me,

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:58.891 align:start size:88% position:13%
whether it was just
some 27-year-old intern

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.660
at the public relations office,

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.829
or whether it was
somebody higher up.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:06.265
A lot of people think it's
somebody perhaps higher up,

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:10.136
who for them, like this is
really bad press, right?

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:11.804 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's obviously
not my goal.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:14.140 align:start size:84% position:16%
My goal is not to
just shit on Trudeau.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.143
My goal is to just say
what I honestly wanna say

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:20.913 align:start position:0%
and talk about some of the
disturbing authoritarian trends

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.548
in this country.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:26.285
And it seemed to have
rung an alarm for them

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:31.190
and they wanted to look into me,

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.693
and I don't know what the
implications of that is,

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:35.828
other than I'm on the
prime minister's radar.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:38.698
And I should probably put
that on my Twitter bio.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:39.932
(Dave laughing)

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.401
- It should be on
your Twitter bio

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:43.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
for as long as you're
allowed to be on Twitter.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:47.240 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know a little something
about how tenuous that can be.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:50.009
But can you just talk like
joking aside for a second?

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:51.277
Can you just talk about the
chilling effect of that?

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.579
I mean, look, you're
outspoken publicly.

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're a young person
trying to make your bones,

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:57.183
make your career.

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.885
You are publicly unvaxxed,

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:01.020
so you could not
leave the country.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.688 align:start size:81% position:19%
You're critical
of the government.

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:05.958 align:start size:97% position:3%
And now you have government
agents in essence

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:08.361
looking closely at your work.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:10.797 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, you're in your
mom's basement, as you said.

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:13.065
It's not the most fun
thing in the world.

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:16.035 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, yeah, no, some
people have mentioned to me

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.970 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I should take this a
bit more seriously than I am.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.306
And I think that's
just my personality

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:23.376
is like, I don't take these
things super, super seriously

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:24.610
and lose sleep over them.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.213
I mean, if Trudeau's
losing sleep over me,

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.414
that's fine enough.

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:29.882
(Dave laughing)

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.818
I don't wanna lose sleep over
making Trudeau lose sleep.

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:36.022 align:start size:97% position:3%
But no, in all seriousness,
it is very chilling

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:38.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
that one article can
have that kind of effect,

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.993
especially given that
I don't really have

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:42.595
like a massive platform yet.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:43.529
I'm still growing.

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.431
I'm still a young person.

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:48.301
And I mean, even
just on Twitter too

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:50.403
with that article that I posted,

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.572
there were so many journalists,

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:54.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
government-funded
journalists by the way,

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:58.277 align:start size:88% position:13%
working for the CBC,
working for Global News,

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:02.181
the Toronto Star that were
pointing out that this op-ed

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.817
is total balderdash and he
should just get vaccinated,

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:07.153
and he just whining
about his freedoms.

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.388 align:start position:0%
And a lot of people, by the
way, weirdly enough were saying,

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:10.823
"Oh, he should just
go back to India.

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:12.291
Why is he even here?"

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:14.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like people like that
were saying and it's like,

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:15.761
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.964 align:start size:88% position:13%
Why did we just go
like Trumpian suddenly?

00:08:17.964 --> 00:08:19.165
Like, why?

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:20.766
Like I thought this
was the rhetoric

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.301
that was associated with Trump.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:24.570
And then that was one of
the points of that essay

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.406
and a couple of other essays
that I've written before too.

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:31.811 align:start position:0%
It's like the direction we
went in, in the name of safety,

00:08:31.811 --> 00:08:34.013
diversity, inclusivity.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:38.784
It's exactly what we feared
would be of the other side.

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:43.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like Trudeau genuinely
has become this monstrous,

00:08:44.891 --> 00:08:46.192 align:start size:84% position:16%
discriminatory
authoritarian leader

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:48.160 align:start size:81% position:19%
that we all feared
Trump would be.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.462
And I'm no Trump defender.

00:08:49.462 --> 00:08:52.298
I'm not gonna defend him
or openly support him,

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.766
or just any of that.

00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:57.003 align:start size:97% position:3%
But what Trudeau is displaying
is true authoritarianism.

00:08:57.003 --> 00:08:59.105
It's true stripping people away

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:02.108 align:start position:0%
from their constitutional rights
and their civil liberties.

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:05.011
And it's, when you're
a young journalist,

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:10.016
I'm definitely not part of
the conventional narrative,

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:13.286 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I'm not
writing for the "CBC."

00:09:13.286 --> 00:09:15.488
I'm not writing for any of
these traditional outlets.

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:17.557
I'm just an independent writer.

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:18.824
And it seems to be,

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:20.526
there's a weird shortage
of that here in Canada.

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:23.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
Otherwise it's mysterious
why I've risen,

00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:25.531 align:start size:84% position:16%
whereas other
journalists haven't.

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:27.867 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's like there aren't enough
independent journalists

00:09:27.867 --> 00:09:29.735
who are willing to say
what I'm willing to say

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:32.071
because they rather get
their journalism degree

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:34.473
and work for the CBC and
get paid a certain salary

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:36.876
and spew out the same
political narrative

00:09:36.876 --> 00:09:38.077
over and over again.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:39.779
But for me, it's like
I don't want to be

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:41.013
anything close to that.

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:43.816
I want to be my own
independent voice

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:46.419 align:start size:88% position:13%
and raise these concerns
about my country.

00:09:46.419 --> 00:09:47.887
- Yeah.

00:09:47.887 --> 00:09:49.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you bring up a
couple interesting things.

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:51.524
I mean, first this idea
that Trudeau in essence

00:09:51.524 --> 00:09:54.760
has become what they
purported Trump to be.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:57.597
Trump, it turned out not
to really be those things

00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:58.798
for all his faults.

